 ```
 
+#### `window-focus`
+
+A transient indicator on the focused window.
+Automatic animation is disabled by default; enable it with `on-focus`.
+The `effect` can be `"flash"` (the default) or `"shrink"`.
+Both work with the focus ring disabled, and with floating and fullscreen windows.
+
+With `effect "flash"`, a tint inside the window fades to transparent.
+The `color` alpha sets the highlight strength.
+The tint follows the window geometry and rounded corners, and stays below its popups.
+
+With `effect "shrink"`, the rendered tile starts smaller around its center and returns to normal size.
+The `scale` sets the starting size and must be greater than 0 and at most 1 (default: 0.98).
+Decorations and popups scale with the window.
+The application size, layout allocation, and pointer hit-testing bounds do not change.
+The scale is clamped between the configured value and 1, including with spring or overshooting curves.
+
+```kdl
+animations {
+    window-focus {
+        on-focus
+        effect "shrink"
+        scale 0.98
+        duration-ms 180
+        curve "ease-out-cubic"
+    }
+}
+binds {
+    Mod+Z { animate-window; }
+}
+```
+
+The `animate-window` action (also `niri msg action animate-window`) works independently of `on-focus`.
+Repeating it restarts the effect; losing keyboard focus cancels it.
+Returning from a launcher or overview counts as gaining focus.
+Both `animations { off; }` and `window-focus { off; }` disable manual and automatic effects.
+Use `on-focus false` to disable only automatic effects.
+Changing this animation's settings cancels any in-progress effect.
+
+`window-focus-flash` and `flash-window` remain compatibility aliases for the configuration block and action.
+The legacy action also plays the selected effect, including shrink.
+If both configuration names occur in the same `animations` block, `window-focus` takes precedence.
+
 #### `window-close`
 
 <sup>Since: 0.1.5</sup>
